---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="The method · borck.consulting" description="How the practice works: find the first move, brief it, check it, keep the judgment, and deliver with a gate.">

  <div class="hero">
    <p class="hero-eyebrow">The method</p>
    <h1 class="hero-title">The method is public. The client work is private.</h1>
    <p class="hero-sub">
      A working sequence for regulated small firms: find the first move, brief it,
      check it, keep the judgement, and set the gate before the pilot.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="section">
    <div class="section-header">
      <span class="section-title">The sequence</span>
    </div>
    <div class="tier-grid">
      <div class="tier-card">
        <div class="tier-card-eyebrow">01 · Find</div>
        <div class="tier-card-title">Find the first move</div>
        <p class="tier-card-desc">
          Spot, assign, prioritise. Start with a quick win that survives a month.
          The Opportunity Finder and the First Move Canvas.
        </p>
        <p><a href="/tools/first-move-canvas/">First Move Canvas →</a></p>
      </div>

      <div class="tier-card">
        <div class="tier-card-eyebrow">02 · Brief</div>
        <div class="tier-card-title">Brief it</div>
        <p class="tier-card-desc">
          Brief AI the way you would brief a capable colleague: role, task, context,
          format, and the check it needs.
        </p>
        <p><a href="/tools/rtcf/">Brief Like You →</a></p>
      </div>

      <div class="tier-card">
        <div class="tier-card-eyebrow">03 · Check</div>
        <div class="tier-card-title">Check the output</div>
        <p class="tier-card-desc">
          Sort the task by consequence and precision. Then raise the flags that tell
          you what to check.
        </p>
        <p>
          <a href="https://trusttool.borck.education">The Trust Tool →</a><br />
          <a href="/writing/the-flag-system">The Flag System →</a>
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="tier-card">
        <div class="tier-card-eyebrow">04 · Keep</div>
        <div class="tier-card-title">Keep the judgement</div>
        <p class="tier-card-desc">
          Conversation, not delegation. The person briefs, pushes back, checks, and
          signs. The tool drafts. The person carries the consequence.
        </p>
        <p>
          <a href="/writing/conversation-not-delegation">The framework →</a><br />
          <a href="https://thehumanedge.borck.dev">The Human Edge →</a>
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="tier-card">
        <div class="tier-card-eyebrow">05 · Deliver</div>
        <div class="tier-card-title">Deliver with a gate</div>
        <p class="tier-card-desc">
          One workflow, one owner, one measure, a named checker, and a 30-day scale,
          pivot, or kill decision written before the pilot.
        </p>
        <p><a href="/services">The AI Readiness Diagnostic →</a></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="section">
    <div class="section-header">
      <span class="section-title">The five questions</span>
    </div>
    <div class="tier-grid">
      <div class="tier-card">
        <div class="tier-card-eyebrow">01</div>
        <div class="tier-card-title">Can we?</div>
        <p class="tier-card-desc">What the firm is actually equipped to take on.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="tier-card">
        <div class="tier-card-eyebrow">02</div>
        <div class="tier-card-title">Should we?</div>
        <p class="tier-card-desc">Where AI creates defensible value, and where it creates more risk than it removes.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="tier-card">
        <div class="tier-card-eyebrow">03</div>
        <div class="tier-card-title">How?</div>
        <p class="tier-card-desc">The sequence, the gates, and the change response.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="tier-card">
        <div class="tier-card-eyebrow">04</div>
        <div class="tier-card-title">Ready?</div>
        <p class="tier-card-desc">Data, infrastructure, talent, and governance.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="tier-card">
        <div class="tier-card-eyebrow">05</div>
        <div class="tier-card-title">Value?</div>
        <p class="tier-card-desc">The business case in the firm's own terms.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="section">
    <div class="section-header">
      <span class="section-title">What is public, what is paid</span>
    </div>
    <div class="tier-grid">
      <div class="tier-card">
        <div class="tier-card-title">Public</div>
        <p class="tier-card-desc">
          The tools, the essays, the field notes, the AI Readiness Reflection, and
          the 30-minute fit call.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="tier-card">
        <div class="tier-card-title">Paid</div>
        <p class="tier-card-desc">
          The Diagnostic, the governance audit, local AI deployment, and
          client-specific work on client data.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="scope-line">
      The method is free because it is the proof. The paid work is the application,
      the client context, and the accountability.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="section">
    <div class="section-header">
      <span class="section-title">Evidence</span>
    </div>
    <p class="hero-sub" style="max-width: none;">
      The method is backed by the lab, the tools, and the teaching record.
      Inspect the <a href="/evidence">evidence</a>, the
      <a href="https://locolabo.org">local-AI lab</a>, the
      <a href="https://research.borck.dev/#cognitive-strategy-transfer">ACIS 2026 paper</a>,
      or the <a href="https://notes.borck.consulting">field notes</a>.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="section">
    <div class="section-header">
      <span class="section-title">Licences and credit</span>
    </div>
    <p class="hero-sub" style="max-width: none;">
      Code and tools are MIT. The books are CC BY 4.0. The field notes are MIT.
      The essays are free to read and share with attribution. Client work and
      private templates are not licensed.
    </p>
    <p style="font-size: 0.85rem; color: var(--gray-1); line-height: 1.7; max-width: 680px;">
      Decide Like You adapts Dylan Davis's Decide Like Me method. The Opportunity
      Finder draws on The Human Edge book and masterclass. The Trust Tool, Brief
      Like You, the Flag System, and Conversation Not Delegation are my own
      working synthesis. Ideas are not copyrightable; the expression is mine.
    </p>
  </div>

</Base>
